## Graph conventions
- Every domain owns ten stable idea IDs.
- Every idea has one owning domain and four explained cross-domain feature connections.
- Domain edges describe product-level dependencies; idea edges identify concrete connected proposals.
- An edge is a design contract, not permission to access another system's private records.
- Read `world_graph.json` for canonical identifiers, rationales, shared invariants and machine-readable structure.
